===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Of, relating, or characteristic of [[writing]] (i.e., of that which has been [[write|written]]).
#: {{ant|en|oral|verbal}}
#: {{rfex|en}}
# Having been written.
#: {{ant|en|unwritten}}
#: {{ux|en|I can speak Japanese fairly well, but I have no understanding whatsoever of '''written''' Japanese.}}

====Quotations====
* {{quote-book|en|title=Writing and Difference|page=62|author=w:Jacques Derrida|coauthors=Alan Bass|year=1978|passage=It is more '''written''' than said}}
* {{quote-book|en|title=Influence and Intertextuality in Literary History|page=109|author=Jay Clayton|coauthors=Eric Rothstein|year=1991|passage=... although certainly more '''written''' than oral, are radically implicated in orality because of their performative nature and susceptibility to "mouvance"}}
* {{quote-book|en|title=The Nixon Memo: Political Respectability, Russia, and the Press|page=68|author=[[w:Marvin Kalb|Marvin L. Kalb]]|year=1994|passage=Strmecki reworked the draft, making it seem "more '''written''' than spoken."}}
* {{quote-book|en|title=The Metamorphosis of English: Versions of Other Languages|page=83|author=Richard M. Swiderski|year=1996|passage=The Chinese is more '''written''' than the English in that the writing is more removed from speech than the phonetic English.}}
* {{quote-book|en|title=Page to Screen: Taking Literacy Into the Electronic Era|page=96|author=Ilana Snyder|coauthors=Michael Joyce|year=1998|passage=Yates concludes that in terms of lexical density, 'CMC users package information in text in ways that are more '''written''' than speech-like'}}
* {{quote-book|en|title=Close Listening: Poetry and the Performed Word|page=211|author=Charles Bernstein|year=1998|passage=printed in caps to suggest that the whole performance be thought of as one gigantic sentence. If Silliman's talk is more '''written''' than spoken, ...}}
* {{quote-book|en|title=Roger Ebert's Movie Yearbook 2004|page=71|author=w:Roger Ebert|year=2003|passage=Even insults, when they are traded, seem more '''written''' than felt.}}

